    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Brady & McCarthy are thrilled to offer 23 Glenamuck Cottages, Carrickmines for Sale. This strikingly beautiful and deceptively spacious four double bedroom split level family home with a feature c.200 ft rear garden is presented to exceptional standards throughout. Originally built in 1910 as a two-bedroom cottage, Number 23 has been substantially extended to now form a superb and generously proportioned family home to include all modern conveniences.\r\n\r\nExtending to a generous c.2,088 Sq.ft / 194 Sq.m, the accommodation comprises an entrance hall, inner hallway with three double bedrooms and shelved hot press. The first floor is presented in landing with bedroom four, the master, featuring an ensuite bathroom and walk through wardrobe, and a shower room. Returning the entrance level, steps lead one to the guest wc, kitchen / breakfast room, open plan living / bar & dining room.\r\n\r\nOutside the home is approached over a gravelled driveway with ample off-street parking. A gated side passageway leads one to the private and substantial rear garden, approx. 200 feet in length which is presented in lawn, hedging and combination of attractively planted borders and mature trees. There is a small courtyard accessed from the kitchen, and the separate utility from the living room. A large timber decked area to the side with a retractable awning lends itself perfectly for al fresco entertaining, and for socialising with family and friends. The mature garden complements the home and creates an idyllic setting for children to play.\r\n\r\nNumber 23 is within easy access of the Carrickmines Retail Park and the bustling villages of Kilternan, Stepaside and Foxrock offering a host of shopping and dining amenities. There are plenty of leisure facilities including Dundrum Town Centre, Sandyford Business Park, Beacon South Quarter and Leopardstown Racecourse, Westwood gym, Carrickmines Lawn Tennis Club, golf clubs, equestrian centres, not to mention an abundance of nearby hill walking and mountain bike routes.\r\n\r\nSome of South County Dublin’s finest schools are nearby including Our Lady of The Wayside, Gaelscoil Thaobh na Coille, Kilternan Church of Ireland NS, Stepaside Educate Together and Rosemount School. Public transportation is plentiful and includes the Luas Green Line and several Bus routes. The M50 and N11 road networks are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nOf interest to prospective purchasers is the substantial rear garden, which may offer exciting potential for the provision of a detached auxiliary dwelling of up to 45 sq.m under the new exempted development provisions being introduced pursuant to the Planning and Development Act 2024, subject to compliance with the relevant conditions. This could create an excellent opportunity for additional family accommodation, a guest suite or other ancillary residential use, further enhancing the flexibility and long term appeal of the property.\r\n\r\nParticular features of Number 23 include the sizeable living accommodation, presentation and generous rear garden. Prospective purchasers could simply enjoy life in their new home from the start. With that, 23 Glenamuck Cottages will no doubt appeal to both First-time buyers and those trading up alike."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hallway \r\nFishbone porcelain tiles, access to the floored attic, shelved hot press.\r\n\r\nGuest WC \r\nTiled floors, wc, whb with brushed nickel sanitary wear, wall mounted mirror, chrome towel heater.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\nDual aspect double bedroom with fitted carpet, wardrobes and television point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\nDouble bedroom with fitted carpet, wardrobes and television point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 \r\nDual aspect double bedroom with fitted carpet, wardrobes and television point.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Breakfast Room \r\nTravertine tiled floor with recessed flooring lighting, generous range of fitted storage units, marble counter tops, Belfast sink with chrome taps, plumbed for dishwasher, Centre island with marble countertop, excellent storage, covered radiator.\r\n\r\nDoors to side courtyard in patio.\r\n\r\nOpen Plan Living / Bar & Dining room.\r\n\r\nLiving room \r\nLight filled room with feature picture window and garden views, timber flooring, television point, panelled walls, integrated speaker system, wood burner stove, access to the side passageway. Bar with marble countertop, mirrored shelving, double doors to side decking. Steps to:\r\n\r\nDining Room \r\nDual aspect twin sliding doors to the rear garden, timber flooring, recessed lighting, feature gas fireplace.\r\n\r\nUtility \r\nPlumed for services.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nLanding \r\nPorcelain tiles, Velux windows x 2.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 – Master \r\nGenerous double bedroom with fitted carpet, Juliette balcony, recessed lighting, television point, walk through wardrobe with generous fitted storage.\r\n\r\nEnsuite \r\nTiled floor, wc, bath, whb with brushed brass fittings, brushed brass heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nShower Room\r\nIlluminated pink marble vanity with brass waterfall shower, brass bidet, wall hung toilet with marble mosaic tile on wall and porcelain tiled floor. Velux window, extractor fan and wired for sound.\r\n\r\nBoiler house."
      },
